et:** Yes, the one-cycle criterion (lines 7070–7086) is similar to your band-crossing budget / upcrossing pigeonhole: a residue class deterministically crosses iff the composed affine map $\\Lambda_k < 1$ AND $B_k < 1 - \\Lambda_k$ (equation 7070–7074). Multi-cycle stacking refines this partition.\n\n---\n\n### 6. ATTACK SURFACE SUMMARY: PROVED VS. OPEN (Lines 11000–11199)\n\n**TABLE 1: Established unconditionally proved results (lines 11018–11064):**\n- Shadow sparsity, shadow return time, finite-depth reduction, hierarchical consistency, monotonicity constraint ✓\n- Repulsion trapping, known-zone memory loss, inherited-bias contraction, harmonic property, constant residual ✓\n- Coding-map injectivity, extension independence, gain-increment independence, rate cancellation ✓\n- No algebraic contraction ($\\tau_B = 1$, isometry, exact harmonicity) ✓\n- Oscillation unboundedness: $\\Theta_K \\to \\infty$ at convergents of $\\log_2 3$ ✓\n- Spectral gain decomposition (band-by-band Walsh), spectral concentration ($\\hw=0,1$ carry $70\\%$–$78\\%$ power) ✓\n\n**TABLE 2: Proved for ensemble, numerical for orbits (lines 11081–11137):**\n- Odd-skeleton reduction, block law, i.i.d. valuations, i.i.d. cycle types ✓\n- Single-cycle crossing ($p_{\\mathrm{cross}} \\approx 0.7137$), one-cycle crossing criterion, universal one-cycle crossing ($P_{\\mathrm{all}} = 0.4194$), two-cycle extension ($61.2\\%$ deterministic) ✓\n- Multi-cycle convergence: $R_k \\approx 0.73 \\cdot 0.75^k$; $82.2\\%$ by $k=5$, extrapolated $R_{20} \\approx 0.002$ ✓\n- Crossing strata: $f_{13} = 0.910$; residual decay $\\approx 0.86^K$ (geometric) ✓\n\n**TABLE 3: Open problems and structural reductions (lines 11152–11195):**\n\n| Open | Content |\n|------|---------|\n| **Amplification Hypothesis** (line 11152–11153) | Orbit hits $S^+(K)$ at most $A^{\\mathrm{cross}}_K \\times$ uniform. **Numerical evidence:** $A_K \\le 2.4$ across 13 orbits (lines 5524–5559), consistent with $A_K = O(1)$. |\n| **Depthwise Recurrence** (line 11154–11155) | Would imply WMH directly. |\n| **Gain-Observable Recurrence** (line 11156–11157) | Weaker target; would imply observable WMH. |\n| **Alignment Renewal** (line 11158–11159) | Missing bridge; would close recurrence. |\n| **Spectral Diffusion** (line 11160–11161) | Would imply Amplification Hypothesis with margin. |\n| **Orbit Covariance Summability** (line 11162–11163) | Would give CLT $\\Rightarrow$ crossing $\\Rightarrow$ Collatz. |\n\n**Route A Status (lines 11172–11173):** CLOSED. Adversarial $n^*$ grows $\\sim e^{0.023k}$; uniformly fragile (Props.~\\ref{prop:adversarial-fragility}, \\ref{prop:general-fragility}).\n\n**Route B Status (lines 11175–11192):** OBSTRUCTED. Bit-generation blocks exhaustion; forced post-Mersenne valuation, burst non-continuation, weak-recovery cylinder, cascade invariant, short-word cylinder. Progress: uniform-fiber gap map, cross-cascade independence, TV reduction, full-cycle fiber map, spectator-bit propagation, exponential tail, TV summability ($\\le 0.028$), cycle contraction, recovery-exit, burst-conditional contraction.\n\n**Route C Status (line 11194–11195):** OBSTRUCTED. Bounding $\\tau(n)$ requires WMH (Rem.~\\ref{rem:crossing-time}, lines 10171–10198).\n\n---\n\n### KEY CONSTANTS AND MARGINS\n\n- **Safety margin:** $4.65\\times$ (Thm.~\\ref{thm:perorbit-gain}, per-orbit gain rate versus $\\varepsilon - R \\approx 0.326$)\n- **Density model:** $R_\\mu(\\rho) \\le 0.142$ for $\\rho \\le 0.63 \\approx 1/\\log_2 3$ (margin $\\ge 65\\%$, Rem.~\\ref{rem:density-model}, line 6077–6080)\n- **Spectral gap:** $\\gamma_{10} = 0.8549$ for fiber-averaged transition matrix on mod-$32$ cascade entries (Prop.~\\ref{prop:exact-spectral-gap}, line 9645)\n- **Chernoff exponent:** $D_* = D(1/\\log_2 3 \\| 1/2) \\approx 0.05004$ (shadow sparsity decay)\n- **TV summability in self-reinforcing loop:** $\\sum_k \\|\\mu_k - \\nu_k\\|_{\\mathrm{TV}} \\le 0.028$ (Thm.~\\ref{thm:mixing-loop}, line 9345)\n- **Non-divergence threshold:** $2^{68}$ (computational verification; above this, mixing loop closes conditional on spectator bits; Rem.~\\ref{rem:nondivergence-threshold}, lines 9692–9741)\n\n---\n\n### COMPARISON TO YOUR PROGRAM\n\nYour \"Syracuse map shadow\" (finite character projections) parallels their \"phantom shadow\" (residue classes at depth $K$). Their **spectral analysis** via Walsh–Hadamard transform on $\\mathbb{Z}/2^K\\mathbb{Z}$ closely parallels your **tilted transfer operator** perspective: both isolate the dominant low-frequency modes (your $\\hw=0,1$ = their band-by-band structure). \n\nTheir **three-lemma programme** (repulsion, memory loss, renewal) mirrors your two-clock renewal structure (burst meter, handoff parity): both decompose the orbit into tractable phases with explicit contraction mechanisms. Their **density model** (odd-step density $\\rho$ governs amplification) resembles your **joint calibration** of depth law and handoff parity.\n\nThe **irreducible hard core** (lines 9871–9878, circularity in their proof): no orbit can sustain patterns that simultaneously grow and exhaust spectator bits—requires understanding carry propagation in $n \\mapsto 3^k n$. This is isomorphic to your open **joint calibration of two scalar channels** (run-depth + handoff parity).","type":"text"}],"prompt":"Read /home/john/mynotes/shadow_frontier/docs/arXiv-2603.11066v6/MAIN_v6_arXiv.tex lines 4653-11300 (section \"Toward the Weak Mixing Hypothesis\": shadow sparsity, repulsion-based shadow return time, finite-depth reduction, hierarchical consistency, depthwise discrepancy recurrence, gain-observable recurrence, first lemmas toward the recurrence, spectral analysis of the gain observable, the odd-skeleton crossing route, modular crossing strata, summary of the attack surface). This is ~6600 lines — sample intelligently: read the start of each subsection (statements, definitions, theorem environments) and the \"summary of the attack surface\" (lines ~11000-11300) fully. 